'''''Dimorphotheca jucunda''''', the '''delightful African daisy''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Asteraceae]]. It is native to South Africa, Lesotho and [[Eswatini]], and introduced to Ireland and [[Tasmania]].<ref name="201475-1" >{{cite web |url=http://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:201475-1 |title=''Dimorphotheca jucunda'' E.Phillips |author=<!--Not stated--> |website=Plants of the World Online |publisher=Board of Trustees of the Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew |access-date=4 June 2021 }}</ref> As its synonym ''Osteospermum jucundum'', it and two of its cultivars, 'Blackthorn Seedling' and 'Langtrees' have gained the [[Royal Horticultural Society]]'s [[Award of Garden Merit]].<ref>{{cite web |title=''Osteospermum jucundum'' delightful African daisy |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/75740/osteospermum-jucundum/details |date=2021 |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=4 June 2021 |quote=Synonyms; ''Osteospermum barberae'' }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=''Osteospermum jucundum'' 'Blackthorn Seedling' African daisy 'Blackthorn Seedling' |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/Plants/49446/i-Osteospermum-jucundum-i-Blackthorn-Seedling/Details |date=2021 |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=4 June 2021 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=''Osteospermum jucundum'' 'Langtrees' African daisy 'Langtrees' |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/Plants/119079/i-Osteospermum-jucundum-i-Langtrees/Details |date=2021 |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=4 June 2021 }}</ref>

